window.QBANK = window.QBANK || [];
window.QBANK.push(
  {"id":"anh11-1-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["br[ea]kfast","m[ea]l","h[ea]lth","pl[ea]sant"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"meal\" /miːl/ có \"ea\" đọc là /iː/; các từ còn lại: breakfast /ˈbrekfəst/, health /helθ/, pleasant /ˈpleznt/ đọc là /e/."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["balance","muscle","diet","routine"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"routine\" /ruːˈtiːn/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; balance /ˈbæləns/, muscle /ˈmʌsl/, diet /ˈdaɪət/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nEating plenty of fruit and vegetables helps boost your ____ system and protects you from infections.","options":["immune","nervous","digestive","solar"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"immune system\" = hệ miễn dịch, giúp chống lại sự nhiễm trùng (infections). Các hệ thần kinh, tiêu hoá không có chức năng này; \"solar system\" là hệ mặt trời."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMy grandfather ____ jogging every morning since he retired.","options":["has gone","went","goes","is going"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Có \"since he retired\" → hành động bắt đầu trong quá khứ, kéo dài đến hiện tại → thì hiện tại hoàn thành: has gone."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nDoctors advise people to ____ sugar and salt to reduce the risk of heart disease.","options":["put up with","take after","cut down on","give in to"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"cut down on\" = cắt giảm. put up with = chịu đựng; take after = giống (ai đó); give in to = nhượng bộ. Chỉ \"cut down on\" hợp nghĩa giảm nguy cơ bệnh tim."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nLast year, Minh ____ 5 kg after he ____ a healthier diet.","options":["has lost / followed","lost / followed","lost / has followed","has lost / has followed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"Last year\" là thời điểm xác định trong quá khứ → dùng quá khứ đơn cho cả hai mệnh đề: lost / followed."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"Do you think I should get more sleep?\"\nB: \"____ Teenagers need about eight to ten hours a night.\"","options":["No, thanks.","Never mind.","Absolutely.","You're welcome."],"answer":2,"explanation":"B đồng ý và đưa ra lí do → \"Absolutely.\" (Chắc chắn rồi). Các phương án khác dùng để từ chối lời mời, an ủi hoặc đáp lại lời cảm ơn."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\n\"____ you ever ____ a marathon?\" – \"No, but I ran a 5 km race last month.\"","options":["Did / run","Have / run","Have / ran","Do / run"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"ever\" hỏi về trải nghiệm tính đến hiện tại → hiện tại hoàn thành: Have you ever run (V3 của run là run)."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nPeople in Okinawa are famous for their ____; many of them live to be over 100.","options":["length","longitude","lengthy","longevity"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"longevity\" = sự sống lâu, tuổi thọ cao, phù hợp với \"live to be over 100\". length = chiều dài; longitude = kinh độ; lengthy là tính từ (dài dòng)."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the part in brackets that needs correction.\nMy uncle [has given] up smoking three years ago, and he [has felt] much [healthier] [since then].","options":["has given","has felt","healthier","since then"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"three years ago\" là mốc quá khứ xác định → phải dùng quá khứ đơn: \"gave up\". Vế sau dùng hiện tại hoàn thành với \"since then\" là đúng."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nRegular exercise is one of the best ways to stay healthy. It strengthens your heart and ____ your muscles, so you feel more energetic during the day.","options":["weakens","tones","damages","reduces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"tone your muscles\" = làm săn chắc cơ bắp, phù hợp với ý tích cực của đoạn văn (strengthens, more energetic). Các từ còn lại mang nghĩa tiêu cực."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nMany young people skip breakfast because they are always in a hurry in the morning. ____, this habit can make them feel tired and lose concentration at school.","options":["Therefore","Moreover","However","Otherwise"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Câu trước nêu lí do bỏ bữa sáng (vì vội), câu sau nêu tác hại – ý tương phản (\"tưởng tiết kiệm thời gian nhưng có hại\") → However. Therefore chỉ kết quả, Moreover bổ sung, Otherwise = nếu không thì."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nScientists have long been curious about why people in certain parts of the world live much longer than average. These places, known as \"Blue Zones\", include Okinawa in Japan, Sardinia in Italy and Nicoya in Costa Rica. Researchers who have studied them found that the people there share several habits. First, they eat mostly plant-based food, such as beans, vegetables and whole grains, and they rarely overeat. Second, they stay physically active throughout the day, not by going to the gym, but by gardening, walking and doing housework. Third, they have strong connections with family and friends, which helps them cope with stress. Finally, many of them have a clear sense of purpose; they wake up every morning knowing why their life matters. Interestingly, genes seem to explain only a small part of their long lives. Most experts now believe that lifestyle choices play a much bigger role.","statements":["People in Blue Zones usually eat a lot of meat.","Most people in Blue Zones keep fit through daily activities rather than by going to the gym.","Strong relationships with family and friends help people in Blue Zones deal with stress.","According to the passage, genes are the main reason for the long lives of people in Blue Zones."],"answer":[false,true,true,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: họ ăn chủ yếu thực phẩm từ thực vật (mostly plant-based food).\nb) Đúng: \"not by going to the gym, but by gardening, walking and doing housework\".\nc) Đúng: \"strong connections with family and friends, which helps them cope with stress\".\nd) Sai: gen chỉ giải thích một phần nhỏ; lối sống đóng vai trò lớn hơn nhiều."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nSleep is just as important for our health as diet and exercise, yet many teenagers do not get enough of it. Experts recommend that people aged 13 to 18 sleep between eight and ten hours a night. However, surveys show that a large number of students sleep fewer than seven hours on school nights. One major reason is the use of smartphones and other screens before bed. The blue light from these devices tricks the brain into thinking it is still daytime, making it harder to fall asleep. Lack of sleep can affect students in many ways. It weakens the immune system, makes it difficult to concentrate in class and can even cause mood swings. To sleep better, teenagers should go to bed at the same time every night, avoid caffeine in the evening and put their phones away at least an hour before sleeping.","statements":["Experts say teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep a night.","Most students sleep more than ten hours on school nights.","Blue light from screens makes it easier for people to fall asleep.","Not getting enough sleep can make it hard for students to focus at school."],"answer":[true,false,false,true],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"sleep between eight and ten hours a night\".\nb) Sai: nhiều học sinh ngủ ít hơn 7 tiếng vào các đêm đi học.\nc) Sai: ánh sáng xanh khiến não tưởng vẫn là ban ngày, làm khó ngủ hơn.\nd) Đúng: thiếu ngủ \"makes it difficult to concentrate in class\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) I started doing yoga three years ago.\n→ I have ...\nb) This is the first time she has tried meditation.\n→ She has never ...\nc) My father last went to the gym two months ago.\n→ My father hasn't ...","answer":"a) I have done (been doing) yoga for three years. b) She has never tried meditation before. c) My father hasn't been (gone) to the gym for two months.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm (sai chính tả/thì trừ 0,5).\na) S + started + V-ing + khoảng thời gian + ago → S + have/has + V3 (have been V-ing) + for + khoảng thời gian.\nb) This is the first time + S + have/has + V3 → S + have/has + never + V3 + before.\nc) S + last + V2 + khoảng thời gian + ago → S + haven't/hasn't + V3 + for + khoảng thời gian (chấp nhận \"been to\" hoặc \"gone to\")."},
  {"id":"anh11-1-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-1","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about the habits a teenager should develop in order to live a long and healthy life. Give reasons or examples to support your ideas.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 2–4 thói quen lành mạnh (ăn uống cân bằng, tập thể dục, ngủ đủ, giữ tinh thần lạc quan…) kèm lí do/ví dụ.","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nIn my opinion, there are several habits that teenagers should develop to live a long and healthy life. First of all, they should follow a balanced diet. Eating plenty of fruit, vegetables and whole grains while cutting down on fast food and sugary drinks gives the body the nutrients it needs. Secondly, regular exercise is essential. Just thirty minutes of jogging, cycling or playing sports a day can strengthen the heart and muscles and reduce stress. Thirdly, teenagers should get enough sleep, ideally eight to ten hours a night, so that their bodies and minds can recover. Finally, keeping a positive attitude and spending time with family and friends are good for mental health. If we start these habits early, we will enjoy better health for many years to come."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["argu[ed]","shar[ed]","respect[ed]","follow[ed]"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"respected\" tận cùng bằng /t/ nên đuôi -ed đọc là /ɪd/; argued, shared, followed tận cùng bằng âm hữu thanh nên -ed đọc là /d/."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["conservative","generation","traditional","experience"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"generation\" /ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃn/ nhấn âm tiết thứ ba; conservative /kənˈsɜːvətɪv/, traditional /trəˈdɪʃənl/, experience /ɪkˈspɪəriəns/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nA ____ family consists of only parents and their children.","options":["extended","nuclear","distant","large"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"nuclear family\" = gia đình hạt nhân (chỉ gồm bố mẹ và con cái). \"extended family\" = gia đình nhiều thế hệ."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nStudents ____ wear uniforms at my school; it is a school rule.","options":["mustn't","don't have to","needn't","have to"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Nội quy trường bắt buộc → \"have to\" (phải). mustn't = cấm; don't have to/needn't = không cần."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMy grandparents have quite ____ views; they think girls should not stay out late at night.","options":["conservative","open-minded","modern","flexible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"conservative\" = bảo thủ, phù hợp với quan điểm cho rằng con gái không nên về khuya. open-minded, modern, flexible đều mang nghĩa cởi mở, trái với ngữ cảnh."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nYou ____ tell anyone about this; it's a family secret.","options":["don't have to","mustn't","needn't","should"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Đây là bí mật gia đình → cấm nói ra → \"mustn't\". don't have to/needn't = không cần (vẫn có thể nói), should = nên – sai nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"I think parents should let teenagers choose their own careers.\"\nB: \"____ It's their life, after all.\"","options":["What a pity!","I'm afraid not.","That's not true.","I couldn't agree more."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Câu sau của B ủng hộ ý kiến của A → \"I couldn't agree more.\" (Tôi hoàn toàn đồng ý). Các phương án khác thể hiện tiếc nuối hoặc phản đối."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nIt's Sunday tomorrow, so I ____ get up early. I can sleep in.","options":["mustn't","have to","don't have to","must"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"I can sleep in\" → không cần dậy sớm → \"don't have to\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nTom decided to follow in his father's ____ and became a doctor like him.","options":["footsteps","footprints","steps","ways"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Thành ngữ \"follow in somebody's footsteps\" = theo bước, nối nghiệp ai đó."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nIt isn't necessary for you to ask for permission to use the family car.","options":["You mustn't ask for permission to use the family car.","You don't have to ask for permission to use the family car.","You should ask for permission to use the family car.","You have to ask for permission to use the family car."],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"It isn't necessary for sb to do sth\" = \"sb doesn't have to do sth\" (không cần). mustn't = cấm, should = nên, have to = phải – đều sai nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nThe generation gap refers to differences in values, attitudes and ____ between young people and older people. It can sometimes lead to conflicts in families.","options":["behave","behaved","behaviour","behaving"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Sau \"values, attitudes and\" cần một danh từ cùng loại → behaviour (hành vi)."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nMany family conflicts arise because each generation grew up in a different environment. To reduce tension, family members should listen to each other and try to ____ the other person's point of view.","options":["ignore","reject","argue about","understand"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Để giảm căng thẳng thì cần lắng nghe và cố gắng \"understand\" (thấu hiểu) quan điểm của người khác; ignore, reject, argue about làm tăng xung đột."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nIn many Vietnamese families, three generations live under the same roof. While this brings many benefits, it can also lead to conflicts. Grandparents, who grew up in a time of hardship, often value saving money and following traditions. Their grandchildren, on the other hand, were born into the digital age. They spend a lot of time online, follow fashion trends and want more freedom to make their own choices. These differences sometimes cause arguments about clothes, careers or how much time to spend on phones. However, the generation gap does not have to divide a family. When young people teach their grandparents to make video calls or use social media, the older generation feels more connected to the modern world. In return, grandparents can share valuable life experience and stories about the past. Mutual respect and open communication are the keys to a happy multigenerational family.","statements":["According to the passage, living with three generations only causes problems.","Grandparents often place a high value on saving money and following traditions.","Young people can help their grandparents feel more connected to the modern world.","The writer believes that respect and good communication can make multigenerational families happy."],"answer":[false,true,true,true],"explanation":"a) Sai: \"this brings many benefits, it can also lead to conflicts\" – có cả lợi ích.\nb) Đúng: \"often value saving money and following traditions\".\nc) Đúng: dạy ông bà gọi video giúp họ \"feels more connected to the modern world\".\nd) Đúng: \"Mutual respect and open communication are the keys to a happy multigenerational family.\""},
  {"id":"anh11-2-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nA recent survey of 500 secondary school students in a big city asked them about the rules their parents set at home. Nearly 70 per cent said they had to finish their homework before using their phones, and more than half said they had to be home before 9 p.m. on weekdays. Many students felt that some rules were reasonable. For example, most agreed that they should help with household chores because everyone in the family shares the home. However, about 40 per cent complained that their parents did not let them choose their own clothes or hairstyles. Interestingly, students who regularly talked with their parents about their problems reported fewer arguments at home. The researchers concluded that rules work best when parents explain the reasons behind them and listen to their children's opinions.","statements":["More than half of the students had to be home before 9 p.m. on weekdays.","Most students thought that helping with household chores was unfair.","About 40 per cent of the students were not allowed to choose their own clothes or hairstyles.","Students who talked to their parents regularly had more arguments at home."],"answer":[true,false,true,false],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"more than half said they had to be home before 9 p.m. on weekdays\".\nb) Sai: phần lớn đồng ý rằng nên giúp việc nhà.\nc) Đúng: \"about 40 per cent complained that their parents did not let them choose their own clothes or hairstyles\".\nd) Sai: những em thường trò chuyện với bố mẹ có ít tranh cãi hơn (fewer arguments)."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) It is necessary for students to switch off their phones during lessons.\n→ Students have to ...\nb) It isn't necessary for you to cook dinner tonight.\n→ You don't ...\nc) Children are not allowed to play with matches.\n→ Children mustn't ...","answer":"a) Students have to switch off their phones during lessons. b) You don't have to (don't need to) cook dinner tonight. c) Children mustn't play with matches.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) It is necessary for sb to do sth = sb has to/must do sth (sự bắt buộc).\nb) It isn't necessary for sb to do sth = sb doesn't have to/doesn't need to do sth (không cần thiết).\nc) be not allowed to do sth = mustn't do sth (sự cấm đoán). Dùng sai \"don't have to\" ở câu c là sai nghĩa, không cho điểm."},
  {"id":"anh11-2-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-2","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about ways to bridge the generation gap in families.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 2–3 cách thu hẹp khoảng cách thế hệ (dành thời gian bên nhau, lắng nghe, tôn trọng, chia sẻ sở thích…).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nThe generation gap is common in many families, but there are several ways to bridge it. First, family members should spend quality time together. Having meals together or going on trips at weekends gives everyone a chance to talk and understand one another better. Second, both generations need to listen with an open mind. Parents should respect their children's choices, while children should understand that their parents' advice comes from experience and love. Third, young people can share their interests with older people, for example, by teaching their grandparents how to use smartphones. In return, they can learn traditional values and life skills from them. In conclusion, with mutual respect and good communication, the generation gap can become a bridge rather than a wall."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["f[u]ture","comm[u]nity","comp[u]ter","p[u]blic"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"public\" /ˈpʌblɪk/ có \"u\" đọc là /ʌ/; future /ˈfjuːtʃə(r)/, community /kəˈmjuːnəti/, computer /kəmˈpjuːtə(r)/ đọc là /juː/."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["infrastructure","sustainable","environment","intelligent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"infrastructure\" /ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃə(r)/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất; sustainable, environment, intelligent nhấn âm tiết thứ hai."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMany cities are building more ____ zones so that people can walk safely without worrying about cars.","options":["industrial","traffic","pedestrian","parking"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"pedestrian zone\" = khu vực dành cho người đi bộ, phù hợp với \"walk safely without worrying about cars\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThis soup ____ delicious. What did you put in it?","options":["is tasting","taste","tastes","are tasting"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"taste\" mang nghĩa \"có vị\" là động từ chỉ trạng thái (stative verb), không dùng tiếp diễn; chủ ngữ số ít → tastes."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nTraffic ____ is a serious problem in big cities during rush hour, when the roads are full of vehicles.","options":["congestion","connection","collection","construction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"traffic congestion\" = tắc nghẽn giao thông, phù hợp với \"roads are full of vehicles\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nBe quiet! The chef ____ the sauce to check if it needs more salt.","options":["tastes","is tasting","has tasted","taste"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Ở đây \"taste\" mang nghĩa \"nếm\" (hành động) nên có thể dùng tiếp diễn; \"Be quiet!\" cho thấy hành động đang diễn ra → is tasting."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"What do you think cities will be like in 2050?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["Yes, I do.","I believe there will be more green spaces and driverless buses.","It was very crowded then.","I have lived in Ha Noi."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Câu hỏi về dự đoán tương lai → trả lời bằng ý kiến về tương lai: \"I believe there will be…\". \"Yes, I do\" không trả lời câu hỏi Wh-; hai phương án còn lại nói về quá khứ/hiện tại."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nI ____ about moving to a smart city after I graduate, but I haven't decided yet.","options":["think","thinks","am thinking","is thinking"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"think about\" mang nghĩa \"cân nhắc\" (hành động) nên dùng được thì tiếp diễn; việc cân nhắc đang diễn ra, chưa quyết định → am thinking."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nCity planners are trying to make the city more ____ by reducing waste and using renewable energy.","options":["sustain","sustainability","sustainably","sustainable"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Sau \"make the city more\" cần tính từ → sustainable (bền vững). sustain là động từ, sustainability là danh từ, sustainably là trạng từ."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the part in brackets that needs correction.\nAt the moment, the city council [is considering] a plan that [is seeming] [very] [promising].","options":["is considering","is seeming","very","promising"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"seem\" là động từ chỉ trạng thái, không dùng thì tiếp diễn → sửa thành \"seems\". \"is considering\" đúng vì consider là động từ hành động."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nIn the cities of the future, most buildings will be powered by ____ energy such as solar and wind power, which will never run out.","options":["fossil","limited","renewable","nuclear"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Năng lượng mặt trời và gió là năng lượng tái tạo (renewable), \"will never run out\" (không bao giờ cạn kiệt)."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nSmart sensors will collect data about traffic and air quality. This information will help the authorities make better decisions ____ the city running smoothly.","options":["to keep","keeping","kept","keep"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Cần cụm chỉ mục đích: \"make better decisions to keep the city running smoothly\" (để giữ cho thành phố vận hành trơn tru) → to keep."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nImagine a city where traffic lights change automatically to reduce traffic jams, rubbish bins tell collectors when they are full, and street lights turn on only when someone walks by. This is what many experts call a \"smart city\". In such a city, sensors collect data about traffic, air quality and energy use. The data is then analysed by computers to help the city run more efficiently. Smart cities are also expected to be greener. Many buildings will have solar panels on their roofs and vertical gardens on their walls, which can clean the air and keep buildings cool. Public transport will be electric, fast and cheap, so fewer people will need private cars. However, building smart cities is very expensive, and some people worry that collecting so much data could put residents' privacy at risk.","statements":["In a smart city, rubbish bins can inform collectors when they need emptying.","Data collected by sensors is used to help the city operate more efficiently.","Vertical gardens make buildings hotter.","Everyone agrees that smart cities have no disadvantages."],"answer":[true,true,false,false],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"rubbish bins tell collectors when they are full\".\nb) Đúng: dữ liệu được phân tích \"to help the city run more efficiently\".\nc) Sai: vườn đứng giúp \"keep buildings cool\".\nd) Sai: thành phố thông minh rất tốn kém và có lo ngại về quyền riêng tư."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nBy 2050, about two thirds of the world's population will live in cities. Feeding so many people will be a big challenge, so urban planners are looking for new ways to grow food. One solution is vertical farming, in which plants are grown in tall buildings on many levels. Instead of soil, the plants grow in water containing nutrients, and LED lights replace sunlight. Vertical farms use up to 95 per cent less water than traditional farms and do not need chemical pesticides. Because they are located inside the city, fresh vegetables can reach supermarkets within hours, which cuts down on transport and pollution. Rooftop gardens are another option. Residents can grow herbs and vegetables on top of their apartment blocks, which also makes the city greener. Although these farms cannot replace traditional agriculture completely, they can play an important role in the cities of the future.","statements":["In vertical farms, plants are usually grown in soil under natural sunlight.","Vertical farming uses much less water than traditional farming.","Food from vertical farms has to travel long distances to reach supermarkets.","The writer thinks vertical farms will completely replace traditional farms."],"answer":[false,true,false,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: cây trồng trong nước chứa chất dinh dưỡng, dùng đèn LED thay ánh nắng.\nb) Đúng: \"use up to 95 per cent less water\".\nc) Sai: trang trại nằm trong thành phố nên rau đến siêu thị \"within hours\".\nd) Sai: \"these farms cannot replace traditional agriculture completely\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) In my opinion, cities of the future will be cleaner.\n→ I think ...\nb) Our city has more parks now than it had ten years ago.\n→ Ten years ago, our city didn't have ...\nc) The smart city project is under consideration by the council at the moment.\n→ The council is ...","answer":"a) I think (that) cities of the future will be cleaner. b) Ten years ago, our city didn't have as many parks as it has (does) now. c) The council is considering the smart city project at the moment.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) \"think\" mang nghĩa \"cho rằng\" (trạng thái) → dùng hiện tại đơn, không dùng \"am thinking\".\nb) So sánh hơn → so sánh không bằng: didn't have as many + N (đếm được số nhiều) + as.\nc) \"be under consideration\" → \"consider\" mang nghĩa \"cân nhắc\" (hành động) → hiện tại tiếp diễn với \"at the moment\": is considering."},
  {"id":"anh11-3-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-3","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) describing the city you would like to live in in 2050.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ mô tả thành phố mơ ước năm 2050 (không gian xanh, giao thông thông minh, năng lượng tái tạo…), dùng các cấu trúc về tương lai/giả định.","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nIn 2050, I would like to live in a green and smart city. First of all, it would have plenty of parks, trees and vertical gardens, so the air would be fresh and clean. Secondly, all public transport would be electric and driverless. People could travel quickly and cheaply by sky trains or electric buses, and there would be no more traffic jams. In addition, every building would use renewable energy from solar panels on its roof, and smart sensors would control lights and air conditioners to save energy. Finally, the city would have safe pedestrian zones and cycle lanes, so residents could walk or cycle to work and school. I believe that living in such a city would make people healthier and happier."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["[ch]arter","[ch]allenge","[ch]aracter","[ch]ampion"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"character\" /ˈkærəktə(r)/ có \"ch\" đọc là /k/; charter, challenge, champion đọc là /tʃ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["organise","community","economy","cooperate"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"organise\" /ˈɔːɡənaɪz/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất; community /kəˈmjuːnəti/, economy /ɪˈkɒnəmi/, cooperate /kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nASEAN's motto is \"One Vision, One ____, One Community\".","options":["Idea","Identity","Interest","Island"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Khẩu hiệu của ASEAN: \"One Vision, One Identity, One Community\" (Một tầm nhìn, Một bản sắc, Một cộng đồng)."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\n____ part in the ASEAN Youth Programme was a great experience for me.","options":["Take","Took","Taking","Taken"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Cần một danh động từ (V-ing) làm chủ ngữ của câu → Taking part in…"},
  {"id":"anh11-4-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe aim of the conference is to ____ cooperation among ASEAN member states in education.","options":["prevent","protest","pretend","promote"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"promote cooperation\" = thúc đẩy hợp tác. prevent = ngăn chặn, protest = phản đối, pretend = giả vờ – sai nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMai is interested in ____ about the cultures of other ASEAN countries.","options":["learning","to learn","learn","learned"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sau giới từ \"in\" (be interested in) dùng V-ing → learning."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"Would you like to join our ASEAN cultural exchange club?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["You're welcome.","I'd love to. When does it meet?","Not at all.","It doesn't matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Đáp lại lời mời một cách tích cực: \"I'd love to.\" (Mình rất thích). Các phương án khác dùng để đáp lời cảm ơn/xin lỗi."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe delegates avoided ____ about sensitive issues during the meeting.","options":["to talk","talking","talk","talked"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Sau động từ \"avoid\" dùng V-ing (gerund làm tân ngữ) → talking."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nStudents from many countries showed great ____ when they took part in the ASEAN quiz competition.","options":["enthusiasm","enthusiastic","enthusiastically","enthusiast"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sau tính từ \"great\" cần danh từ chỉ sự vật trừu tượng → enthusiasm (sự nhiệt tình). enthusiast là danh từ chỉ người (người đam mê) – không hợp nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the part in brackets that needs correction.\n[Representing] my school at the ASEAN quiz [made] me feel proud, and I look forward to [take] part in it [again] next year.","options":["Representing","made","take","again"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"look forward to\" – \"to\" là giới từ nên theo sau là V-ing → sửa \"take\" thành \"taking\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nASEAN was founded in 1967 by five countries. Since then, its membership has more than doubled. The association aims ____ peace, stability and economic growth in the region.","options":["promoting","promote","promoted","to promote"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Cấu trúc \"aim to do sth\" (nhằm mục đích làm gì) → aims to promote."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nThe ASEAN Youth Volunteer Programme brings together young people from across the region. Volunteers not only help local communities ____ also learn a lot about different cultures.","options":["and","or","but","so"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Cấu trúc tương quan \"not only … but also …\" (không những … mà còn …) → but."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nThe Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) was established on 8 August 1967 in Bangkok, Thailand. Its five founding members were Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand. Over the following decades, more countries joined the association. Viet Nam became the seventh member in July 1995, an important step in the country's international integration. ASEAN's motto, \"One Vision, One Identity, One Community\", shows the members' wish to work closely together. In 2015, the ASEAN Community was officially formed, built on three pillars: political-security, economic and socio-cultural cooperation. Since joining, Viet Nam has played an active role in the organisation. It has held the rotating chairmanship several times and hosted many important meetings. Membership has also brought Viet Nam many benefits, such as greater trade with its neighbours, more foreign investment and more opportunities for students to study and work in the region.","statements":["ASEAN was founded by five countries.","Viet Nam was one of the founding members of ASEAN.","The ASEAN Community is based on three pillars.","According to the passage, joining ASEAN has brought Viet Nam few benefits."],"answer":[true,false,true,false],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"Its five founding members were…\".\nb) Sai: Việt Nam là thành viên thứ bảy, gia nhập năm 1995.\nc) Đúng: \"built on three pillars\".\nd) Sai: tư cách thành viên mang lại \"many benefits\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nLast summer, Linh, a grade 11 student from Da Nang, took part in a two-week ASEAN youth camp in Malaysia. The camp brought together 60 students from different Southeast Asian countries. At first, Linh felt nervous because she had never travelled abroad on her own. However, she soon made friends with students from Thailand, Indonesia and the Philippines. Every day, the participants attended workshops on topics such as climate change, digital skills and cultural diversity. They also worked in mixed teams to plan a community project. Linh's team designed a campaign to reduce plastic waste in schools, and it won the best project award. In the evenings, each country group performed traditional songs and dances. Linh and her friends introduced the audience to the Vietnamese conical hat and taught them a folk song. Linh says that taking part in the camp improved her English and made her feel proud of being an ASEAN citizen.","statements":["Linh had travelled abroad alone many times before the camp.","The participants worked in teams that included students from different countries.","Linh's team won an award for a project about saving water.","Taking part in the camp helped Linh improve her English."],"answer":[false,true,false,true],"explanation":"a) Sai: \"she had never travelled abroad on her own\".\nb) Đúng: \"worked in mixed teams\" – các nhóm gồm học sinh nhiều nước.\nc) Sai: dự án về giảm rác thải nhựa (reduce plastic waste), không phải tiết kiệm nước.\nd) Đúng: \"taking part in the camp improved her English\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) It is interesting to learn about the cultures of other ASEAN countries.\n→ Learning ...\nb) My sister likes to make friends with students from other countries.\n→ My sister is fond of ...\nc) \"We should send more students on exchange programmes,\" said the teacher.\n→ The teacher suggested ...","answer":"a) Learning about the cultures of other ASEAN countries is interesting. b) My sister is fond of making friends with students from other countries. c) The teacher suggested sending more students on exchange programmes.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) It is + adj + to V → V-ing (danh động từ làm chủ ngữ) + is + adj; động từ chia số ít.\nb) be fond of + V-ing (danh động từ làm tân ngữ của giới từ).\nc) suggest + V-ing (chấp nhận: suggested that they (should) send…)."},
  {"id":"anh11-4-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-4","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about the benefits that Viet Nam's membership of ASEAN brings to Vietnamese young people.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 2–4 lợi ích (cơ hội du học, việc làm, chương trình giao lưu thanh niên, hiểu biết văn hoá…).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nBeing a member of ASEAN brings many benefits to young people in Viet Nam. Firstly, it gives them more opportunities to study abroad. Many universities in the region offer scholarships and exchange programmes for Vietnamese students. Secondly, young people can find jobs more easily in other member states, because ASEAN encourages the free movement of skilled workers. Thirdly, joining youth programmes such as camps, competitions and volunteer activities helps them improve their English, develop teamwork skills and make friends from neighbouring countries. Finally, learning about the cultures of other nations helps young Vietnamese people become more open-minded and respectful of differences. In short, ASEAN membership opens many doors for the young generation, and they should make the most of these chances."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["cl[i]mate","r[i]se","em[i]ssion","w[i]ldlife"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"emission\" /iˈmɪʃn/ có \"i\" đọc là /ɪ/; climate /ˈklaɪmət/, rise /raɪz/, wildlife /ˈwaɪldlaɪf/ đọc là /aɪ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["carbon","release","atmosphere","temperature"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"release\" /rɪˈliːs/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; carbon /ˈkɑːbən/, atmosphere /ˈætməsfɪə(r)/, temperature /ˈtemprətʃə(r)/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nBurning ____ fuels such as coal and oil releases large amounts of carbon dioxide.","options":["solar","fossil","renewable","green"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Than và dầu là nhiên liệu hoá thạch → fossil fuels."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe ice ____ in the Arctic is causing sea levels to rise.","options":["melts","melted","to melt","melting"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Mệnh đề quan hệ rút gọn dạng chủ động (the ice which is melting) → hiện tại phân từ: melting."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nCutting down forests, also known as ____, reduces the Earth's ability to absorb carbon dioxide.","options":["deforestation","afforestation","desertification","urbanisation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"deforestation\" = nạn phá rừng. afforestation = trồng rừng (ngược nghĩa); desertification = sa mạc hoá; urbanisation = đô thị hoá."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMost of the electricity ____ in this country comes from coal-fired power plants.","options":["producing","produced","produces","is produced"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Điện \"được sản xuất\" → nghĩa bị động → mệnh đề quan hệ rút gọn bằng quá khứ phân từ: produced (= which is produced)."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"What can we do to reduce our carbon footprint?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["Yes, we can.","The carbon footprint is very big.","We can use public transport instead of cars.","I don't know where it is."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Câu hỏi xin giải pháp → đưa ra gợi ý cụ thể: \"We can use public transport instead of cars.\""},
  {"id":"anh11-5-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nPeople ____ near the coast are most at risk from rising sea levels.","options":["living","lived","are living","who living"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mệnh đề quan hệ rút gọn chủ động (people who live/are living near the coast) → living."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nGreenhouse gases ____ heat in the atmosphere, causing the Earth's temperature to rise.","options":["release","reflect","trap","cool"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Khí nhà kính \"giữ\" nhiệt trong khí quyển → trap heat, dẫn đến nhiệt độ tăng."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences.\nThe report was published last week. It warns that global temperatures may rise by 1.5°C.","options":["The report publishing last week warns that global temperatures may rise by 1.5°C.","The report was published last week warns that global temperatures may rise by 1.5°C.","Having published last week, the report warns that global temperatures may rise by 1.5°C.","The report published last week warns that global temperatures may rise by 1.5°C."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Bản báo cáo \"được xuất bản\" → nghĩa bị động → rút gọn bằng quá khứ phân từ: The report published last week… (= which was published)."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nGlobal warming leads to more extreme weather events, such as heatwaves, droughts and ____. In some places, heavy rain can cover whole villages with water.","options":["sunshine","floods","breezes","rainbows"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Thời tiết cực đoan, mưa lớn làm ngập cả làng → floods (lũ lụt)."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nThe polar ice caps are melting faster than ever before. ____, many coastal cities may be under water by the end of this century.","options":["As a result","In contrast","However","For example"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Băng tan nhanh dẫn đến kết quả là nhiều thành phố ven biển có thể bị ngập → As a result (Kết quả là)."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nThe Earth is surrounded by a layer of gases called the atmosphere. Some of these gases, such as carbon dioxide and methane, act like the glass walls of a greenhouse. They let sunlight in but trap some of the heat that the Earth gives off, keeping our planet warm enough for life. This natural process is called the greenhouse effect. Without it, the average temperature on Earth would be well below freezing. The problem is that human activities are adding more greenhouse gases to the atmosphere. Burning coal, oil and gas for electricity and transport releases huge amounts of carbon dioxide, while cutting down forests means fewer trees are left to absorb it. Farming, especially raising cattle, also produces a lot of methane. As a result, more heat is trapped and the planet is getting warmer. This is what scientists call global warming.","statements":["The natural greenhouse effect makes life on Earth possible.","Without the greenhouse effect, the Earth would be much hotter than it is today.","Cutting down forests reduces the amount of carbon dioxide that can be absorbed.","Raising cattle produces large amounts of methane."],"answer":[true,false,true,true],"explanation":"a) Đúng: hiệu ứng nhà kính tự nhiên giữ Trái Đất \"warm enough for life\".\nb) Sai: không có nó, nhiệt độ trung bình sẽ \"well below freezing\" (lạnh hơn nhiều).\nc) Đúng: \"fewer trees are left to absorb it\".\nd) Đúng: \"raising cattle, also produces a lot of methane\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nViet Nam is one of the countries most affected by global warming. The Mekong Delta, often called the country's \"rice bowl\", is especially at risk. Because much of the delta is only one or two metres above sea level, rising seas allow salt water to flow further inland, particularly in the dry season. This saltwater intrusion damages rice fields and fruit orchards and makes fresh drinking water harder to find. At the same time, the country is experiencing more frequent and stronger storms, floods and heatwaves. To adapt, many farmers in the delta have switched from growing rice to raising shrimp or growing crops that can survive in salty soil. The government has also built dykes and planted mangrove forests along the coast to protect people's homes. However, experts say that these efforts must go together with cutting greenhouse gas emissions around the world.","statements":["The Mekong Delta is located high above sea level.","Salt water flowing inland damages crops in the Mekong Delta.","Some farmers have changed what they grow or raise to adapt to salty conditions.","According to experts, building dykes alone is enough to solve the problem."],"answer":[false,true,true,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: phần lớn đồng bằng chỉ cao hơn mực nước biển 1–2 mét.\nb) Đúng: xâm nhập mặn \"damages rice fields and fruit orchards\".\nc) Đúng: nông dân chuyển sang nuôi tôm hoặc trồng cây chịu mặn.\nd) Sai: các chuyên gia cho rằng phải đi kèm với cắt giảm khí thải toàn cầu."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) The man who is standing next to the poster is a climate scientist.\n→ The man standing ...\nb) The trees which were planted by our class last year are growing well.\n→ The trees planted ...\nc) Because she felt worried about global warming, Lan started cycling to school.\n→ Feeling ...","answer":"a) The man standing next to the poster is a climate scientist. b) The trees planted by our class last year are growing well. c) Feeling worried about global warming, Lan started cycling to school.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) Mệnh đề quan hệ chủ động → rút gọn bằng V-ing (bỏ who is).\nb) Mệnh đề quan hệ bị động → rút gọn bằng V3/ed (bỏ which were).\nc) Mệnh đề trạng ngữ chỉ nguyên nhân cùng chủ ngữ, chủ động → cụm hiện tại phân từ: Feeling…, chủ ngữ Lan giữ ở mệnh đề chính."},
  {"id":"anh11-5-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-5","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about what students can do to help reduce global warming.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 3–4 hành động cụ thể của học sinh (tiết kiệm điện, đi xe đạp/xe buýt, giảm–tái sử dụng–tái chế, trồng cây, tuyên truyền…).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nGlobal warming is one of the biggest problems facing our planet, but students like me can help to reduce it in several simple ways. First, we can save energy at home and at school by turning off lights, fans and computers when we are not using them. Second, instead of asking our parents to take us to school by motorbike, we can walk, cycle or take the bus, which reduces the amount of carbon dioxide released into the air. Third, we should reduce, reuse and recycle. Using fewer plastic bags and bottles means less energy is needed to produce them. Finally, we can plant trees and join environmental clubs to raise awareness among our friends. If every student makes small changes, together we can make a big difference."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["herit[a]ge","vill[a]ge","cott[a]ge","st[a]ge"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"stage\" /steɪdʒ/ có \"a\" đọc là /eɪ/; heritage /ˈherɪtɪdʒ/, village /ˈvɪlɪdʒ/, cottage /ˈkɒtɪdʒ/ đọc là /ɪ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["heritage","monument","preserve","festival"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"preserve\" /prɪˈzɜːv/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; heritage, monument /ˈmɒnjumənt/, festival /ˈfestɪvl/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nHa Long Bay was recognised by UNESCO as a World ____ Site.","options":["History","Heritage","Habitat","Holiday"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Cụm cố định \"World Heritage Site\" = Di sản Thế giới."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nNeil Armstrong was the first person ____ on the Moon.","options":["to walk","walking","walked","walk"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sau \"the first/the last/the only + N\" dùng to-infinitive để thay cho mệnh đề quan hệ → the first person to walk."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nLocal people are working hard to ____ the ancient temple, which was badly damaged in the storm.","options":["destroy","remove","replace","restore"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"restore\" = trùng tu, khôi phục (công trình bị hư hại). destroy = phá huỷ, remove = dỡ bỏ, replace = thay thế – không phù hợp."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe Complex of Hue Monuments was the first site in Viet Nam ____ as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO.","options":["to recognise","to be recognised","recognising","recognise"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Sau \"the first + N\" dùng to-infinitive; quần thể \"được công nhận\" → bị động: to be recognised."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"How about organising a clean-up day at the old pagoda?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["I'm sorry to hear that.","Congratulations!","That sounds like a great idea!","Don't mention it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Đáp lại lời đề nghị (How about…?) bằng sự đồng tình: \"That sounds like a great idea!\""},
  {"id":"anh11-6-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nShe was the only student in our class ____ the essay competition about local heritage.","options":["won","to win","wins","win"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Sau \"the only + N\" dùng to-infinitive → the only student to win (= who won)."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nQuan ho folk songs are an example of ____ cultural heritage because they are passed down orally, not as physical objects.","options":["intangible","tangible","natural","visible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"intangible heritage\" = di sản phi vật thể (không phải vật thể hữu hình), phù hợp với \"passed down orally, not as physical objects\". tangible = vật thể."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nLan was the last visitor who left the museum.","options":["Lan was the last visitor left the museum.","Lan was the last visitor to leaving the museum.","Lan was the last visitor that leaving the museum.","Lan was the last visitor to leave the museum."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Rút gọn mệnh đề quan hệ sau \"the last + N\" bằng to-infinitive: the last visitor to leave."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nMany young people today are not interested in learning traditional crafts, so some craft villages are in danger of ____.","options":["developing","growing","disappearing","appearing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Giới trẻ không quan tâm → làng nghề có nguy cơ \"biến mất\" → disappearing."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nTourism can bring money to heritage sites, which can be used for restoration. ____, too many visitors can damage old buildings and pollute the area.","options":["As a result","On the other hand","Therefore","In addition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Câu trước nêu lợi ích, câu sau nêu tác hại → ý đối lập: On the other hand (Mặt khác)."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nHoi An Ancient Town in central Viet Nam was recognised as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1999. From the 15th to the 19th century, it was a busy trading port where merchants from Japan, China and Europe came to buy and sell goods. Today, the town still has more than a thousand old buildings, including wooden houses, pagodas, family chapels and the famous Japanese Covered Bridge. What makes Hoi An special is that these buildings are not just museums; many of them are still homes and shops where local people live and work. In recent years, the number of tourists has increased rapidly. Although tourism brings jobs and income, it also creates problems such as overcrowding, noise and rubbish. To protect the town, the local authorities limit traffic in the old quarter, and visitors are encouraged to buy tickets which help pay for the restoration of old buildings.","statements":["Hoi An used to be an important trading port.","All the old buildings in Hoi An are now empty museums.","Tourism has brought both benefits and problems to Hoi An.","Traffic in the old quarter is not controlled at all."],"answer":[true,false,true,false],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"it was a busy trading port\".\nb) Sai: nhiều ngôi nhà vẫn là nơi người dân sống và buôn bán.\nc) Đúng: du lịch mang lại việc làm, thu nhập nhưng gây quá tải, ồn ào, rác thải.\nd) Sai: chính quyền \"limit traffic in the old quarter\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nIntangible cultural heritage includes traditions such as music, festivals, crafts and spoken stories that are passed from one generation to the next. Viet Nam has many such treasures recognised by UNESCO, including Nha nhac (Hue royal court music), Quan ho Bac Ninh folk songs and Ca tru singing. However, these art forms face many challenges today. Many young people prefer pop music and find traditional performances old-fashioned. In addition, some of the most experienced artists are now very old, and few young people are willing to spend years learning from them. To keep these traditions alive, several clubs have been set up to teach young people traditional singing for free. Some young musicians are also mixing folk melodies with modern music and sharing their songs on social media. Thanks to these efforts, a growing number of teenagers are becoming interested in their country's musical heritage.","statements":["Intangible heritage includes things like festivals and spoken stories.","Ca tru is one of the Vietnamese traditions recognised by UNESCO.","Most young people today prefer traditional music to pop music.","Combining folk melodies with modern music has made some teenagers more interested in traditional music."],"answer":[true,true,false,true],"explanation":"a) Đúng: di sản phi vật thể gồm \"music, festivals, crafts and spoken stories\".\nb) Đúng: Ca trù được nêu trong danh sách được UNESCO công nhận.\nc) Sai: nhiều bạn trẻ thích nhạc pop và thấy biểu diễn truyền thống lỗi thời.\nd) Đúng: nhờ các nỗ lực đó, ngày càng nhiều thiếu niên quan tâm đến di sản âm nhạc."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) He was the first student who arrived at the museum.\n→ He was the first student to ...\nb) The Complex of Hue Monuments was the first site in Viet Nam that UNESCO recognised as a World Heritage Site.\n→ The Complex of Hue Monuments was the first site in Viet Nam to be ...\nc) She is the youngest artist who has performed Ca tru on this stage.\n→ She is the youngest artist to ...","answer":"a) He was the first student to arrive at the museum. b) The Complex of Hue Monuments was the first site in Viet Nam to be recognised as a World Heritage Site (by UNESCO). c) She is the youngest artist to have performed (to perform) Ca tru on this stage.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\nSau the first/the last/the only/so sánh nhất + N, mệnh đề quan hệ được rút gọn bằng to-infinitive.\na) Chủ động: to + V.\nb) Bị động: to be + V3.\nc) Hành động đã xảy ra trước: to have + V3 (chấp nhận \"to perform\")."},
  {"id":"anh11-6-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-6","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about what young people can do to preserve the cultural heritage of Viet Nam.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 3–4 việc giới trẻ có thể làm (tìm hiểu di sản, ứng xử có trách nhiệm khi tham quan, quảng bá trên mạng xã hội, học nghề/nghệ thuật truyền thống…).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nPreserving our heritage is the responsibility of everyone, especially young people. First, we should learn more about our cultural heritage by visiting museums, historical sites and craft villages. The more we understand it, the more we will value it. Second, we must behave responsibly when visiting heritage sites. We should not litter, write on walls or touch fragile objects. Third, young people can use social media to promote heritage. For example, we can post photos and short videos about famous places or traditional festivals to attract both local and foreign visitors. Finally, we can join clubs that teach traditional arts such as folk singing or making pottery, so that these skills are passed on to future generations. If we all take action, our heritage will be kept alive for many years to come."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["appli[ed]","graduat[ed]","enroll[ed]","train[ed]"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"graduated\" tận cùng bằng /t/ nên -ed đọc là /ɪd/; applied, enrolled, trained có -ed đọc là /d/."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["degree","career","ensure","college"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"college\" /ˈkɒlɪdʒ/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất; degree /dɪˈɡriː/, career /kəˈrɪə(r)/, ensure /ɪnˈʃʊə(r)/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nAfter finishing secondary school, Nam went to a ____ school to train as a car mechanic.","options":["vocational","primary","nursery","boarding"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"vocational school\" = trường dạy nghề, phù hợp với việc học làm thợ sửa ô tô."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\n____ finished his exams, Minh went on holiday with his family.","options":["Had","Having","Have","Has"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Cụm phân từ hoàn thành \"Having + V3\" diễn tả hành động xảy ra trước hành động ở mệnh đề chính → Having finished."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMany students take a ____ year to travel or work before going to university.","options":["leap","spare","gap","free"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"gap year\" = năm nghỉ (giữa phổ thông và đại học) để đi du lịch, làm việc."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nShe was proud of ____ a scholarship to study in Australia.","options":["to have win","having been won","win","having won"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Sau giới từ \"of\" dùng danh động từ; việc giành học bổng xảy ra trước → danh động từ hoàn thành chủ động: having won."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"I'm not sure whether to go to university or start an apprenticeship.\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["Why don't you talk to a career adviser?","Yes, I am.","Congratulations!","It's very kind of you."],"answer":0,"explanation":"A đang phân vân → B đưa ra lời khuyên: \"Why don't you talk to a career adviser?\""},
  {"id":"anh11-7-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe student was accused of ____ in the final exam.","options":["to cheat","having cheated","cheated","having been cheated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"accuse sb of + V-ing; hành động gian lận xảy ra trước việc bị buộc tội và mang nghĩa chủ động → having cheated."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nUniversity graduates often have better career ____ than those without a degree.","options":["prosperity","prospective","prospects","prospectors"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"career prospects\" = triển vọng nghề nghiệp. prosperity = sự thịnh vượng; prospective là tính từ; prospectors = người tìm quặng."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences.\nHe completed the course. Then he applied for a job at a bank.","options":["Having completed the course, he applied for a job at a bank.","Completed the course, he applied for a job at a bank.","Having been completed the course, he applied for a job at a bank.","To have completed the course, he applied for a job at a bank."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Hai hành động cùng chủ ngữ, hành động hoàn thành khoá học xảy ra trước, mang nghĩa chủ động → Having + V3: Having completed the course, …"},
  {"id":"anh11-7-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nHigher education is not the only path to success. Vocational training provides students ____ the practical skills that employers need.","options":["for","to","of","with"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Cấu trúc \"provide sb with sth\" (cung cấp cho ai cái gì) → with."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nAn apprenticeship is a good option for school-leavers who want to start working early. It allows young people to earn money ____ they are learning a trade.","options":["unless","because","while","although"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Hai hành động diễn ra đồng thời (vừa kiếm tiền vừa học nghề) → while (trong khi)."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nEvery year, thousands of Vietnamese school-leavers face an important decision: should they go to university or choose vocational training? For many families, a university degree is still seen as the only path to a good job. However, this view is beginning to change. Vocational schools offer shorter courses, usually lasting from several months to three years, and the tuition fees are often lower. Students spend most of their time practising real skills, such as repairing cars, cooking, designing websites or caring for patients. As a result, many of them can find jobs soon after graduating. On the other hand, a university education provides deeper academic knowledge and can lead to careers that require a degree, such as medicine, law or research. Experts advise students to think carefully about their interests, abilities and the job market before deciding, rather than simply following their friends or their parents' wishes.","statements":["All Vietnamese families now believe that vocational training is better than university.","Vocational courses are usually shorter than university courses.","Vocational students mainly study theory rather than practise skills.","Experts advise students to base their choice on their own interests and abilities."],"answer":[false,true,false,true],"explanation":"a) Sai: với nhiều gia đình, bằng đại học vẫn được coi là con đường duy nhất; quan niệm chỉ \"beginning to change\".\nb) Đúng: khoá học nghề ngắn, từ vài tháng đến ba năm.\nc) Sai: học sinh học nghề dành phần lớn thời gian thực hành kĩ năng.\nd) Đúng: chuyên gia khuyên cân nhắc sở thích, năng lực và thị trường lao động."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nAfter finishing high school, Hung did not go straight to university like most of his classmates. Instead, he took a gap year. For the first six months, he worked as a waiter in a hotel in Nha Trang to save money. He then spent three months volunteering at a primary school in a mountainous area, where he taught English to children. During his gap year, Hung learned many things that he could not learn from books. He became more confident, learned how to manage his own money and discovered that he loved working with children. When he came back, he applied to a teacher training university and was accepted. Hung's parents were worried at first because they thought a gap year was a waste of time. Now they believe that it helped their son choose the right career.","statements":["Hung went to university immediately after leaving high school.","Hung worked in a hotel to earn money during his gap year.","Hung's experience as a volunteer helped him discover his interest in teaching.","Hung's parents supported his gap year from the very beginning."],"answer":[false,true,true,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: Hung không vào đại học ngay mà nghỉ một năm (gap year).\nb) Đúng: làm bồi bàn ở khách sạn để tiết kiệm tiền.\nc) Đúng: dạy tiếng Anh tình nguyện giúp cậu nhận ra mình yêu thích làm việc với trẻ em, sau đó thi vào trường sư phạm.\nd) Sai: lúc đầu bố mẹ lo lắng, cho rằng đó là lãng phí thời gian."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) After he had passed the entrance exam, he moved to Ha Noi.\n→ Having ...\nb) She regrets that she didn't apply for the scholarship.\n→ She regrets not ...\nc) He denied that he had copied his friend's assignment.\n→ He denied ...","answer":"a) Having passed the entrance exam, he moved to Ha Noi. b) She regrets not having applied (not applying) for the scholarship. c) He denied having copied (copying) his friend's assignment.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) Hai mệnh đề cùng chủ ngữ, hành động trước dùng thì quá khứ hoàn thành → cụm phân từ hoàn thành Having + V3.\nb) regret + (not) having + V3: hối tiếc vì đã (không) làm gì (chấp nhận \"not applying\").\nc) deny + having + V3 (chấp nhận \"copying\")."},
  {"id":"anh11-7-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-7","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about the education option you would like to choose after leaving school and explain why.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu lựa chọn (đại học, học nghề, học việc, gap year…) và 2–3 lí do rõ ràng.","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nAfter leaving school, I would like to go to university to study information technology. There are several reasons for my choice. Firstly, I have always been interested in computers and coding. I spend a lot of my free time learning how to build simple websites and apps, so studying IT would allow me to develop my passion. Secondly, IT graduates have good career prospects. Many companies in Viet Nam and abroad need skilled programmers, and the salaries are attractive. Thirdly, a university degree will give me deep academic knowledge as well as chances to do research and take part in exchange programmes. Although university tuition fees are quite high, I plan to apply for scholarships and work part-time to support myself. I believe this choice will help me achieve my dreams."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["m[o]ney","h[o]me","l[o]ve","d[o]ne"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"home\" /həʊm/ có \"o\" đọc là /əʊ/; money /ˈmʌni/, love /lʌv/, done /dʌn/ đọc là /ʌ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["budget","manage","rely","money"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"rely\" /rɪˈlaɪ/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; budget, manage, money nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nDoing household ____ like cooking and cleaning helps teenagers become more independent.","options":["chores","choirs","chairs","charts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"household chores\" = việc nhà (nấu ăn, dọn dẹp…)."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nIt was my mother ____ taught me how to manage my pocket money.","options":["which","what","who","whom"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Câu chẻ nhấn mạnh chủ ngữ chỉ người: It was + người + who/that + V → who. \"whom\" chỉ dùng cho tân ngữ."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nGood ____ management helps students balance their schoolwork and free time.","options":["money","anger","stress","time"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Cân bằng giữa việc học và thời gian rảnh → time management (quản lí thời gian)."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nIt is in this small flat ____ I learned to live on my own.","options":["where","that","which","who"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Câu chẻ nhấn mạnh trạng ngữ chỉ nơi chốn: It is + in this small flat + that + mệnh đề. Đã có giới từ \"in\" nên không dùng where/which."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"Could you show me how to use the washing machine?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["No, I can't, thanks.","You're welcome.","Not at all, I did it.","Sure. First, you put the clothes in here."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Đáp lại lời nhờ giúp đỡ bằng sự đồng ý và hướng dẫn: \"Sure. First, you put the clothes in here.\""},
  {"id":"anh11-8-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nIt was not until I moved to the city ____ I learned to cook for myself.","options":["when","then","that","which"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Cấu trúc câu chẻ: It was not until + thời gian/mệnh đề + that + S + V (mãi đến khi… mới…) → that."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nBeing ____ means being able to do things and make decisions without help from others.","options":["self-reliant","self-conscious","selfish","self-centred"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"self-reliant\" = tự lực, tự lập. self-conscious = e dè, ngại ngùng; selfish = ích kỉ; self-centred = chỉ biết đến bản thân."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nMy father taught me to ride a bike.","options":["It was my father whom taught me to ride a bike.","It was my father who taught me to ride a bike.","It was my father which taught me to ride a bike.","It was my father what taught me to ride a bike."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Câu chẻ nhấn mạnh chủ ngữ chỉ người: It was + my father + who/that + V. \"whom\" không làm chủ ngữ; which/what không dùng cho người."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nLearning to manage a budget is an important life skill. Teenagers should keep ____ of how much money they spend each week, so they don't run out before the end of the month.","options":["trace","touch","trail","track"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Cụm \"keep track of\" = theo dõi, ghi lại."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nIndependent people are not afraid of making mistakes. ____, they see mistakes as chances to learn and grow.","options":["Instead","Besides","Otherwise","Similarly"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"Instead\" (thay vào đó): thay vì sợ sai lầm, họ coi sai lầm là cơ hội học hỏi. Besides = ngoài ra; Otherwise = nếu không thì; Similarly = tương tự."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nBecoming independent does not happen overnight; it is a process that starts in the teenage years. One of the first steps is learning to take care of yourself. This means doing household chores such as cooking simple meals, washing clothes and keeping your room tidy. Another important skill is managing money. Teenagers who receive pocket money can practise making a budget, saving for things they want and avoiding buying things on impulse. Time management is also essential. Independent learners plan their schedules, set priorities and do not wait for their parents or teachers to remind them about deadlines. Finally, being independent means being able to make decisions and take responsibility for them. Of course, this does not mean that teenagers should never ask for help. In fact, knowing when and whom to ask for advice is a sign of maturity.","statements":["According to the passage, people become independent suddenly when they turn 18.","Making a budget can help teenagers avoid buying things on impulse.","Independent learners rely on their teachers to remind them of deadlines.","The writer thinks that asking for advice is a sign of being immature."],"answer":[false,true,false,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: tự lập \"does not happen overnight\", là một quá trình bắt đầu từ tuổi thiếu niên.\nb) Đúng: lập ngân sách, tiết kiệm và \"avoiding buying things on impulse\".\nc) Sai: họ \"do not wait for their parents or teachers to remind them\".\nd) Sai: biết khi nào và hỏi ai để xin lời khuyên là \"a sign of maturity\" (dấu hiệu trưởng thành)."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nWhen Thao moved from her hometown in Nghe An to Ha Noi to study at university, she lived on her own for the first time. During the first month, everything seemed difficult. She spent most of her monthly allowance in the first two weeks and had to eat instant noodles for days. She also often stayed up late chatting online and then overslept, missing several morning classes. Realising that things had to change, Thao decided to make a plan. She wrote down all her expenses in a notebook and set a weekly spending limit. She learned to cook simple, healthy meals, which was much cheaper than eating out. She also set an alarm and put her phone away at 11 p.m. every night. After three months, Thao felt much more confident. She now says that living away from home has taught her lessons that no classroom could teach.","statements":["Thao had lived alone before she moved to Ha Noi.","In the first month, Thao ran out of money quickly.","Cooking at home helped Thao save money.","Thao still misses her morning classes because she oversleeps."],"answer":[false,true,true,false],"explanation":"a) Sai: \"she lived on her own for the first time\".\nb) Đúng: tiêu gần hết tiền trợ cấp trong hai tuần đầu, phải ăn mì gói.\nc) Đúng: nấu ăn \"much cheaper than eating out\".\nd) Sai: cô đã đặt báo thức, cất điện thoại lúc 11 giờ tối và trở nên tự tin hơn – việc ngủ quên là chuyện của tháng đầu."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) Lan's grandmother gave her the first piece of advice about saving money.\n→ It was Lan's grandmother ...\nb) I learned to manage my time at university.\n→ It was at university ...\nc) I didn't become confident until I started living on my own.\n→ It was not until ...","answer":"a) It was Lan's grandmother who (that) gave her the first piece of advice about saving money. b) It was at university that I learned to manage my time. c) It was not until I started living on my own that I became confident.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) Nhấn mạnh chủ ngữ chỉ người: It was + N + who/that + V.\nb) Nhấn mạnh trạng ngữ nơi chốn: It was + at university + that + S + V.\nc) S + didn't + V + until… → It was not until + mệnh đề + that + S + V (khẳng định, quá khứ đơn)."},
  {"id":"anh11-8-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-8","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) explaining why teenagers should learn to be independent.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ nêu 2–3 lí do (chuẩn bị cho cuộc sống trưởng thành, tăng sự tự tin, giảm gánh nặng cho cha mẹ…).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nIn my opinion, it is very important for teenagers to learn to be independent. Firstly, independent teenagers are better prepared for adult life. When they go to university or start working, they will have to cook, manage money and solve problems on their own. Learning these life skills early will help them avoid many difficulties later. Secondly, independence builds confidence. When young people make their own decisions and take responsibility for them, they feel more mature and believe in their own abilities. Thirdly, being independent reduces the burden on parents, who are often busy with work. Of course, teenagers can still ask their families for advice when necessary. In short, becoming independent is a valuable process that helps teenagers grow into responsible and successful adults."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["so[c]ial","spe[c]ial","offi[c]ial","vi[c]tim"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"victim\" /ˈvɪktɪm/ có \"c\" đọc là /k/; social, special, official có \"c\" đọc là /ʃ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["support","pressure","poverty","victim"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"support\" /səˈpɔːt/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; pressure, poverty, victim nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMany teenagers feel ____ pressure to dress or behave like their friends.","options":["pair","peer","pear","pier"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"peer pressure\" = áp lực đồng trang lứa. Các từ còn lại là từ đồng âm/gần âm: pair (đôi), pear (quả lê), pier (bến tàu)."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\n____ the bad weather, the anti-bullying campaign went ahead as planned.","options":["Although","Because","Despite","However"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Sau chỗ trống là cụm danh từ (the bad weather) và hai vế tương phản → Despite + N. Although cần mệnh đề; However là trạng từ liên kết."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nPosting cruel comments about someone online is a form of ____.","options":["cyberbullying","cybercafe","cyberspace","cybersecurity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Đăng bình luận ác ý về ai đó trên mạng là \"cyberbullying\" (bắt nạt qua mạng)."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nShe didn't report the problem to her teacher ____ she was afraid of being laughed at.","options":["although","so","despite","because"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Vế sau là nguyên nhân của vế trước, có mệnh đề đầy đủ → because."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"I think schools should teach students how to deal with stress.\"\nB: \"____ Many students are under a lot of pressure these days.\"","options":["Not at all.","You're absolutely right.","What a shame!","Thank you."],"answer":1,"explanation":"B bổ sung lí do ủng hộ ý kiến → \"You're absolutely right.\" (Bạn hoàn toàn đúng)."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nPoverty is a serious problem in some remote areas. ____, many children there cannot go to school.","options":["However","Although","As a result","In contrast"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Nghèo đói dẫn đến hậu quả trẻ không được đi học → As a result (Do đó, kết quả là)."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe campaign aims to raise ____ of the harmful effects of body shaming.","options":["aware","awareness","awake","unaware"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Cụm \"raise awareness of sth\" = nâng cao nhận thức về điều gì; cần danh từ → awareness."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences.\nLan was a victim of bullying. She never gave up her studies.","options":["Although Lan was a victim of bullying, she never gave up her studies.","Because Lan was a victim of bullying, she never gave up her studies.","Despite Lan was a victim of bullying, she never gave up her studies.","Lan was a victim of bullying, so she never gave up her studies."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Hai vế tương phản → Although + mệnh đề. \"Despite\" không đi với mệnh đề; because/so chỉ quan hệ nhân quả – sai nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nSpending too much time on social media can lead to ____ health problems such as anxiety and depression.","options":["medal","metal","mantle","mental"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Lo âu và trầm cảm là vấn đề sức khoẻ tinh thần → mental health."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nStudents who are bullied often lose their self-esteem and feel lonely. ____, some of them may even refuse to go to school.","options":["In contrast","Nevertheless","In some cases","On the contrary"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Câu sau nêu hậu quả nghiêm trọng hơn xảy ra với một số người → In some cases (Trong một số trường hợp). Các phương án còn lại diễn tả sự đối lập – không phù hợp."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nCyberbullying is bullying that takes place on digital devices such as phones and computers. It can include sending hurtful messages, spreading rumours online, sharing embarrassing photos or deliberately leaving someone out of online groups. Unlike traditional bullying, cyberbullying can happen at any time of the day or night, and harmful posts can spread to a large audience within minutes. Because bullies can hide behind fake accounts, victims often do not know who is attacking them. The effects can be serious. Victims may feel lonely, anxious or depressed, and their schoolwork may suffer. Experts advise victims not to reply to the bully, but to save the evidence by taking screenshots, block the person and report the problem to a trusted adult. Schools and parents also have an important role to play in teaching young people to use the internet safely and respectfully.","statements":["Cyberbullying can only happen during school hours.","Harmful posts online can reach many people very quickly.","Victims are advised to reply to the bully immediately.","Taking screenshots can help victims keep evidence of cyberbullying."],"answer":[false,true,false,true],"explanation":"a) Sai: \"can happen at any time of the day or night\".\nb) Đúng: \"can spread to a large audience within minutes\".\nc) Sai: chuyên gia khuyên \"not to reply to the bully\".\nd) Đúng: \"save the evidence by taking screenshots\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nPeer pressure is the influence that people of the same age have on one another. It is a normal part of growing up, and it is not always negative. For example, friends who study hard can encourage you to do better at school, and a friend who plays sport may persuade you to join a team. However, peer pressure can also push teenagers into making bad choices, such as skipping classes, smoking or spending too much money to fit in with a group. Many young people find it difficult to say no because they are afraid of being laughed at or left out. To deal with negative peer pressure, teenagers should choose friends who share their values and learn to say no politely but firmly. It is also helpful to talk to parents or teachers when they feel stressed. Remember that true friends will respect your decisions.","statements":["Peer pressure can sometimes have a positive effect.","Teenagers never find it hard to refuse their friends.","Choosing friends with similar values can help teenagers deal with negative peer pressure.","According to the passage, true friends will respect your choices."],"answer":[true,false,true,true],"explanation":"a) Đúng: \"it is not always negative\", có thể khuyến khích học tốt, chơi thể thao.\nb) Sai: \"Many young people find it difficult to say no\".\nc) Đúng: nên \"choose friends who share their values\".\nd) Đúng: \"true friends will respect your decisions\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) Although he was under a lot of pressure, he did well in the exam.\n→ Despite ...\nb) Their families are poor, so many children have to leave school early.\n→ Because of ...\nc) The campaign was well organised. However, few students joined it.\n→ Although ...","answer":"a) Despite being under a lot of pressure (Despite the pressure), he did well in the exam. b) Because of their families' poverty (Because of being poor), many children have to leave school early. c) Although the campaign was well organised, few students joined it.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) Although + mệnh đề → Despite + V-ing/cụm danh từ.\nb) so (chỉ kết quả) → Because of + cụm danh từ chỉ nguyên nhân (poverty là danh từ của poor).\nc) However nối hai câu tương phản → Although + mệnh đề, mệnh đề (bỏ However)."},
  {"id":"anh11-9-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-9","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) about a social issue that teenagers face today (e.g. social media addiction, bullying, peer pressure). Describe its effects and suggest some solutions.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ: nêu vấn đề, 2 tác hại, 2–3 giải pháp, có câu kết.","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nOne of the most serious social issues facing teenagers today is social media addiction. Many young people spend hours scrolling through social networks every day, which causes several problems. Firstly, it takes time away from studying, sleeping and doing physical activities, so their health and school results may suffer. Secondly, constantly comparing themselves with others online can lower their self-esteem and lead to anxiety. To solve this problem, teenagers should set daily time limits on their apps and turn off notifications while studying. Parents should also encourage their children to take part in sports, clubs and outdoor activities. In addition, schools can organise talks to raise students' awareness of the harmful effects of overusing social media. With these efforts, teenagers can enjoy technology in a healthier way."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-01","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word whose part in brackets is pronounced differently from that of the others.","options":["heal[th]y","ear[th]","wea[th]er","ma[th]s"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"weather\" /ˈweðə(r)/ có \"th\" đọc là /ð/; healthy, earth, maths có \"th\" đọc là /θ/."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-02","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Pronunciation","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the word that differs from the other three in the position of primary stress.","options":["habitat","species","balance","extinct"],"answer":3,"explanation":"\"extinct\" /ɪkˈstɪŋkt/ nhấn âm tiết thứ hai; habitat /ˈhæbɪtæt/, species /ˈspiːʃiːz/, balance /ˈbæləns/ nhấn âm tiết thứ nhất."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-03","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nA ____ is the natural home of an animal or a plant.","options":["habit","habitat","harbour","harvest"],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"habitat\" = môi trường sống tự nhiên của động/thực vật. habit = thói quen; harbour = bến cảng; harvest = vụ thu hoạch."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-04","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Which of the following words is a compound noun?","options":["wildlife","wildly","wilder","wildness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"wildlife\" = wild + life là danh từ ghép (động vật hoang dã). wildly là trạng từ, wilder là tính từ so sánh hơn, wildness là danh từ phái sinh (có hậu tố -ness)."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-05","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe variety of plant and animal life in a particular area is called ____.","options":["biology","biography","biodiversity","biomass"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"biodiversity\" = đa dạng sinh học. biology = sinh học; biography = tiểu sử; biomass = sinh khối."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-06","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"practice","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nTwo of my ____ work as rangers at Cuc Phuong National Park.","options":["brother-in-laws","brothers-in-laws","brother-in-law","brothers-in-law"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Danh từ ghép có gạch nối dạng N + giới từ + N: thêm -s vào danh từ chính (brother) → brothers-in-law."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-07","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Speaking & Communication","type":"mcq","level":"NB","difficulty":1,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the most suitable response to complete the exchange.\nA: \"What can we do to protect the local wetland?\"\nB: \"____\"","options":["Yes, it is.","We could organise a clean-up and stop people from dumping rubbish there.","It's very kind of you.","Thanks a lot."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Câu hỏi xin giải pháp → đưa ra đề xuất cụ thể: \"We could organise a clean-up…\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-08","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nThe ____ in Cat Tien National Park help protect the animals from illegal hunters.","options":["parks rangers","parks ranger","park ranger","park rangers"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Danh từ ghép N + N: danh từ đứng trước giữ dạng số ít, chỉ danh từ chính được chia số nhiều; động từ \"help\" chia số nhiều → park rangers."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-09","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Vocabulary","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the best option to complete the sentence.\nMany species are in danger of ____ because their habitats are being destroyed.","options":["extinction","extinct","distinction","instinct"],"answer":0,"explanation":"\"in danger of extinction\" = có nguy cơ tuyệt chủng; sau giới từ \"of\" cần danh từ → extinction. distinction = sự khác biệt; instinct = bản năng."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-10","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Grammar","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Choose the part in brackets that needs correction.\n[Coral reefs] are home [to] thousands of [specie] of fish and other [sea creatures].","options":["Coral reefs","to","specie","sea creatures"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"species\" (loài) có dạng số ít và số nhiều giống nhau; không có dạng \"specie\" với nghĩa này → sửa thành \"species\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-11","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nIn an ecosystem, living things such as plants and animals ____ with non-living things like water, soil and sunlight. Together they form a complex network.","options":["interrupt","introduce","interact","interfere"],"answer":2,"explanation":"\"interact with\" = tương tác với. Sinh vật sống tương tác với các yếu tố không sống để tạo thành một mạng lưới."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-12","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Reading","type":"mcq","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and choose the best option to fill in the blank.\nEvery living thing in a food chain depends on others. If one species disappears, the whole ecosystem can be seriously ____.","options":["affected","effected","affecting","effecting"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Câu bị động (can be + V3) và nghĩa \"bị ảnh hưởng\" → affected. \"effect\" (động từ) nghĩa là \"tạo ra, thực hiện\" – sai nghĩa."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-13","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nMangrove forests grow along tropical coastlines where the land meets the sea. Their trees have special roots that allow them to survive in salty water and in soil that is flooded twice a day by the tide. Mangroves are among the most valuable ecosystems on Earth. They provide a habitat for many species of fish, crabs, birds and monkeys. Their thick roots act as a natural wall, protecting coastal villages from storms and preventing the land from being washed away. Mangroves also store large amounts of carbon, helping to slow down global warming. In Viet Nam, the Can Gio Mangrove Forest near Ho Chi Minh City was almost completely destroyed during the war. Thanks to a replanting programme that started in the late 1970s, it has recovered and was recognised by UNESCO as a World Biosphere Reserve in 2000.","statements":["Mangrove trees can survive in salty water.","Mangroves provide homes only for fish.","Mangrove roots help protect coastal villages from storms.","The Can Gio Mangrove Forest has never been damaged."],"answer":[true,false,true,false],"explanation":"a) Đúng: rễ đặc biệt giúp cây \"survive in salty water\".\nb) Sai: là nơi sống của cá, cua, chim và khỉ.\nc) Đúng: rễ dày như bức tường tự nhiên bảo vệ làng ven biển khỏi bão.\nd) Sai: rừng Cần Giờ gần như bị phá huỷ hoàn toàn trong chiến tranh."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-14","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Reading","type":"tf","level":"TH","difficulty":2,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n\nCoral reefs cover less than one per cent of the ocean floor, yet they are home to about a quarter of all marine species. For this reason, they are often called the \"rainforests of the sea\". A coral reef is built by tiny animals called coral polyps, which live together with algae. The algae provide the corals with food and give them their bright colours. However, coral reefs are in serious danger. When the sea becomes too warm, the corals push out the algae and turn white, a process known as coral bleaching. If the water does not cool down soon, the corals may die. Pollution, overfishing and careless tourism also damage reefs. Because so many species depend on coral reefs, their loss would affect the whole ocean ecosystem and the millions of people who rely on reefs for food and income.","statements":["Coral reefs cover a large part of the ocean floor.","Coral polyps are tiny plants.","Coral bleaching happens when sea water becomes too warm.","Many people depend on coral reefs for food and income."],"answer":[false,false,true,true],"explanation":"a) Sai: rạn san hô chiếm chưa đến 1% đáy đại dương.\nb) Sai: polyp san hô là những động vật nhỏ (tiny animals).\nc) Đúng: \"When the sea becomes too warm… coral bleaching\".\nd) Đúng: \"millions of people who rely on reefs for food and income\"."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-15","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Rewrite each sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the original one, beginning with the words given.\na) If we don't protect the wetlands, many birds will lose their habitats.\n→ Unless ...\nb) People cut down trees in the rainforest every day.\n→ Trees in the rainforest ...\nc) The ranger works in the national park. He is my uncle.\n→ The ranger who ...","answer":"a) Unless we protect the wetlands, many birds will lose their habitats. b) Trees in the rainforest are cut down every day. c) The ranger who works in the national park is my uncle.","explanation":"Mỗi câu đúng: 1 điểm.\na) If … not = Unless (mệnh đề sau Unless ở dạng khẳng định).\nb) Câu bị động thì hiện tại đơn: are + V3 (cut down), bỏ \"by people\".\nc) Nối hai câu bằng mệnh đề quan hệ \"who\" thay cho chủ ngữ chỉ người \"he\" (chấp nhận \"that\")."},
  {"id":"anh11-10-16","subject":"anh","grade":11,"chapter":"anh11-10","topic":"Writing","type":"essay","level":"VD","difficulty":3,"pool":"exam","source":"Tự biên soạn","content":"Write a paragraph (about 120 words) explaining why we should protect ecosystems and what we can do to protect them.","answer":"Đoạn văn khoảng 120 từ: 2 lí do cần bảo vệ hệ sinh thái và 2–3 biện pháp (của chính phủ và cá nhân).","explanation":"Gợi ý chấm (10 điểm): bố cục câu chủ đề – các ý hỗ trợ – câu kết (3 điểm); nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ/lí do (3 điểm); từ vựng đúng chủ đề (2 điểm); ngữ pháp, chính tả, liên kết câu (2 điểm).\nBài mẫu:\nEcosystems such as forests, wetlands and coral reefs are extremely important, so we must protect them. First of all, they provide habitats for millions of plant and animal species. When an ecosystem is destroyed, many species may become endangered or even extinct, and the balance of nature is broken. Second, healthy ecosystems give humans clean air, fresh water, food and medicine. Forests absorb carbon dioxide and help reduce global warming, while mangroves protect coastal areas from storms. To protect ecosystems, governments should create more national parks and pass strict laws against illegal logging and hunting. As individuals, we can reduce waste, avoid buying products made from endangered animals and join tree-planting activities. If we act now, we can keep our ecosystems healthy for future generations."}
);
